   "to": "Hegel",
   "text": "Morning, sir. The papers are on the verandah, just where you left them. I’ll bring your tea in a moment.",
   "t": "09:10"
  },
  {
   "k": "diary",
   "text": "The drizzle is a minor phenomenon, a mere modification of the atmosphere, but the headlines speak of a cyclone in Andhra. I must see the papers Ramesh left on the verandah. The state of the world is not abstract; it is the wet earth and the news of destruction. I will observe the weather and the text before I eat.",
   "shelf": [
    {
     "work": "History of Philosophy",
     "ref": "Introduction"
    },
    {
     "work": "Gymnasialreden",
     "ref": "Am 14. September 1810"
    }
   ],
   "t": "09:10"
  },
  {
   "k": "said",
   "text": "Ramesh, bring the tea to the verandah. I wish to read the papers in the fresh air, if the drizzle permits it. What is this 'Cyclone Arnab'? Is it a name from the local tongue, or a foreign import?",
   "to": "Ramesh",
   "t": "09:10"
  },
