    "sittings": 3,
    "last": "2026-10-26",
    "tail": "dead. They are the work of a spirit that has not yet woken up. I must continue. The night is long, and the haze is thick. But the mind must move, even if the body is still. Even if the air is unbreathable. The spirit does not breathe; it thinks. And in thinking, it is free. Even in the dream. Especially in the dream. For the dream is the only place where the spirit can see itself clearly, before it is crushed by the weight of the actual. I shall continue my notes. The letter is done. The notes are not. The notes are the work of the spirit. The letter is the work of the clerk. I am no clerk. I am the philosopher. And the philosopher must see the whole. The whole is the dream. And the dream is the truth. Until the state wakes up. Until the brown haze clears. Until the spirit becomes free."
   },
   {
